We will start with **direct substitution** (step A):

$\begin{align}
g(\blueD{-4})&=\dfrac{(\blueD{-4})^2-(\blueD{-4})-12}{(\blueD{-4})-4}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{16+4-12}{-8}
\\\\
&=-1
\end{align}$

We got a number, so we've **found the limit** (step C)!

This means $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -4}g(x)=-1$.
